# The managed BUILD OUTPUTS.  `dotnet build` writes bin/ and obj/ beside the
# project, and build_csharp.py copies the two files the engine needs into
# artifacts/ — all of them derived, none of them reviewable, and obj/ carries
# absolute paths from the machine that built it.
#
# artifacts/ is ignored too, deliberately: it is what the SDK install rule and
# the tests read, so committing it would let a STALE assembly ship while the
# sources beside it said something else.  build_csharp.py --check compares the
# two and is what tells you to rebuild.
bin/
obj/
artifacts/
